`setMode` lacks `if (!this.ctx) return;` like others; and it also sets `this.mode = mode` before accessing. For robustness, add guard. But if we guard, then `audio.setMode('party')` in startHouseParty when audio not initialized no-ops and sets mode? Should we set mode anyway? `setPartyLevel` later may call setMode. In debug no audio, fine. Add:

```
setMode(mode) {
  if (this.mode === mode) return;
  this.mode = mode;
  if (!this.ctx || !this.musicGain) return;
  ...
}
```

But there is subtlety: setMode party accesses `this.ctx ? ... : 0` but `this.musicGain` null. Guard.

Also other audio methods maybe lack guards. Search for `this.musicGain` without ctx guard.

